      "content": "Thanks for the breakdown. I'm looking at some industry reports and it seems like the \"stay neutral\" strategy is becoming a lot harder to pull off because consumers are increasingly expecting brands to have a purpose. \n\nIf we choose to stay neutral, isn't there a real risk that being seen as \"indifferent\" will actually be interpreted as being \"against\" the reform by our main customer base? Basically, is neutrality even a viable strategy anymore, or is it just a way to lose both sides?",
